            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "CULLY79"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I changed this just a bit, so I can't give it 5 stars. I added 8 ozs. of sour cream to stretch it a bit and make it more creamy. I also add about 2 Tbs. of zesty cocktail sauce and a tablespoon of lemon juice to add the zip other posters said was lacking. I brought it to work for a low-carb potluck and served with whole wheat crackers. Everyone really liked it."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Tready"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I am living near the Gulf of Mexico. We buy live crabs and boil them in Crab Boil. Crab Boil is all spices which enhance the flavor of the ordinarily bland tasting crab meat. Also, in the boil we add onions and lemons along with small red potatoes and corn on the cob. These veggies also absorb the flavors of the crab boil. The shrimp are done in similar fashion, but boil a lot shorter time. The result is the same. So, whenever I find a recipe that calls for canned seafood, I substitute the home made variety and it turns out well. So folks, use some spices in the recipe and maybe the canned variety will take on a new flavor, as some of you have done.",
            "datePublished": "2013-12-21T12:16:47.190Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "lwilson97"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This turned out really tasty but I made several changes. I blended 8 oz of cream cheese with 1/4 cup of chili sauce as recommended by other reviewers. Added the one green onion and two cans of canned crab instead of just one. I don't like canned shrimp, so I bought 1/2 lb. of fresh and steamed it myself with vinegar and Old Bay, then chopped it up. Other reviewers kept stating this needed a \"kick.\" I think I figured out what is missing - about 1-2 tsp of Old Bay seafood seasoning. This was great served with crackers after chilliing.",
            "datePublished": "2010-01-16T14:33:28.423Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "LA Forrest"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Turned out great but I lessened the crab meat to 6oz and added old bay &amp; Cajun seasoning for more flavor and spice.",
            "datePublished": "2020-03-31T03:44:05.610Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Deborah Merkle"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I make this dip but I use 2 cans of shrimp, a regular small onion chopped fine instead of the green onions and I add seasoning salt (or Trader Joe's 21 seasoning salute if I have it) and course ground pepper. It is always a hit and ends up being the recipe everyone asks for.",
            "datePublished": "2009-01-07T12:15:39.587Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was my first time using canned shrimp and canned Bumble Bee crab. I chose this recipe because it was so easy and inexpensive to make, but I found it tasteless. However, I read the reviews and added the horseradish and Tabasco, and that fixed it right up! I also recommend letting the mixture sit in the fridge for a bit to allow the flavors to come out.",
            "datePublished": "2013-12-31T15:28:16.550Z"
          },
          {
